  "_dayOfWeekComment": [
    "The -1 cases are the multi-hall guard, and they are the load-bearing ones here.",
    "An event id for a second hall is `${dateKey}__${locationId}`, so an id reaches this",
    "function that is not a date. Before the guard, '2026-08-07__somerville'.split('-')",
    "gave [2026, 8, NaN] -> Invalid Date -> NaN, and NaN is in no daysOfWeek array, so",
    "coversDate said false. That reads as THE DATE LOST ITS SABHA, and sabhaRecurrence's",
    "reconcileDate cancels the rides of a date that lost its sabha. A whole hall's evening",
    "of Bhulka would have been cancelled by a scheduler with nothing in the logs.",
    "-1 rather than null so the return stays a number and every caller keeps compiling;",
    "no real day-of-week is negative, so it can never match a configured day."
  ],
  "_effectiveEventForComment": [
    "hall exception -> date exception -> rule, for ONE hall on one date.",
    "A hall exception is only ever an override: both halls run the same evening, so a hall",
    "document says 'not this hall tonight' or 'this hall at a different time'. It never",
    "conjures a gathering on a date the congregation is not meeting, which is why the",
    "inert-on-a-quiet-date cases below matter as much as the ones that change something.",
    "",
    "Every scheduled hall exception here carries BOTH times, because normaliseException",
    "refuses a scheduled exception that does not (line 149) \u2014 a one-field snapshot",
    "normalises to null, which would make these cases pass by testing nothing at all.",
    "venue and agenda are the fields that genuinely fall back, and they are covered."
  ],
